.TH SDL_HINT_AUDIO_FREQUENCY 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_AUDIO_FREQUENCY \- A variable controlling the default audio frequency.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_AUDIO_FREQUENCY \(dqSDL_AUDIO_FREQUENCY\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If the application doesn\(aqt specify the audio frequency when opening the device, this hint can be used to specify a default frequency that will be used\[char46] This defaults to \(dq44100\(dq\[char46]
.PP
This hint should be set before an audio device is opened\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

